                <pb facs="0127" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg62"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/4208: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1936-04-30T14:00:00-04:00"
                            notBefore="1936-04-29T00:00:00+02:35">undated</date>].<lb/>[Received
                        April 30, 1936—2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>253. My 250, April 29.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d67-f1"/> The Emperor has been in
                    close seclusive touch with officials of the Government here during the past day
                    or two and is even believed to have spent a night in Addis Ababa. Government had
                    made preparations to leave tonight but is evidently not leaving before tomorrow.
                    The Italians are reported at Debra Berhan about 75 miles from here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
